ghelper-linux (0.4.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fix Fans and Power reading the last profile's EPP instead of the
    active profile's EPP, and guard programmatic VerticalSlider range
    clamping from triggering unintended PPT writes.
  * Add live temperature/RPM overlay and readout on fan charts, plus a
    Fan Profiles status indicator (BIOS default / Custom active /
    Unsaved changes).
  * Support a third MID fan (chart, hwmon fan3 readout and curve presets)
    and the fPPT (PL3) slider when exposed by firmware.

 -- Atlas <atlas@hypertextcoffee.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:58:00 -0500

ghelper-linux (0.4.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Sync profile changes and AC/battery transitions with tuned-ppd /
    power-profiles-daemon (org.freedesktop.UPower.PowerProfiles) so
    TuneD's balanced-battery profile does not overwrite asusd on unplug.
  * Subscribe directly to asusd PlatformProfile and UPower OnBattery
    D-Bus signals with transition and settle guards to eliminate stale
    UI state and mid-switch flicker.
  * Increment tray dbusmenu layout revisions on updates, initialize
    dbus-glib thread locks, and include PowerProfiles status in --check.

 -- Atlas <atlas@hypertextcoffee.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:15:00 -0500

ghelper-linux (0.4.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Support refresh-rate switching on GNOME (Mutter D-Bus), Hyprland
    (hyprctl) and wlroots compositors (wlr-randr), and decouple Panel
    Overdrive when refresh-rate control is unavailable.
  * Read temperature and power from active proprietary NVIDIA dGPUs via
    NVML without waking runtime-suspended GPUs.
  * Add ROG Slash Lighting and AniMe Matrix controls via asusd D-Bus in
    the main window, Settings and --check diagnostics.

 -- Atlas <atlas@hypertextcoffee.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:57:00 -0500

ghelper-linux (0.3.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Attach the GLib main loop before the first session-bus connection.  The
    KWin placement helper now runs at startup, before the tray module, and was
    leaving dbus-python with a connection that could not export the tray icon.
  * With no tray, the application also quit when started with --minimized or
    closed to the tray; both work again.
  * Regression tests import the app, the tray and the KWin helper in separate
    processes and assert the default main loop is set.

 -- Atlas <atlas@hypertextcoffee.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:05:00 -0500

ghelper-linux (0.3.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Centre the mode card on the whole screen and place it near the bottom
    edge; a side panel no longer pushes it off-centre.
  * Load the KWin placement watcher at startup so the first card after a
    launch is positioned too.

 -- Atlas <atlas@hypertextcoffee.com>  Fri, 20 Nov 2026 10:40:00 -0500

ghelper-linux (0.3.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Remember the chosen performance mode per power source; asusd restores it
    when the cable is plugged or pulled, even while the window is closed.
  * Show a small bottom-centre card naming the mode after a power-source
    change, and after a hotkey or tray switch while the window is hidden.
  * Settings shows which mode is remembered for AC and for battery.
  * --profile updates the same per-source memory.
  * One shared profile name/icon table for the windows, the card and the CLI.

